'''''Begonia hirtella''''', the '''bearded begonia''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Begoniaceae]].<ref name="RHS_203443" >{{cite web |title=''Begonia hirtella'' (S) |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/203443/begonia-hirtella-(s)/details |date=2023 |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=6 July 2023 }}</ref> It is native to Jamaica, Venezuela, Colombia, Peru, Bolivia, and southern Brazil, and has been introduced to many tropical locales around the world.<ref name="POWO_104855-1" >{{cite POWO |id=104855-1 |title=''Begonia hirtella'' Link |access-date=6 July 2023 }}</ref> People apply its juices to their skin to treat itchiness from insect bites.<ref>{{citation |title=Potensi Daun Trembilungan (''Begonia hirtella'' Link) sebagai Antibakteri dan Antifungi |year=2017 |last1=Ngazizah |first1=Febri Nur |last2=Ekowati |first2=Nuraeni |last3=Septiana |first3=Aisyah Tri |journal=Biosfera |volume=33 |issue=3 |page=126 |doi=10.20884/1.mib.2016.33.3.309 |doi-access=free }}</ref>
